  "note": "Election of the Cookstown Urban District Council, ordinary day 15 May 1939; the four retiring members were the only persons nominated and were re-elected (Mid-Ulster Mail, 13 May 1939, p. 4). 'The four retiring members of Cookstown Urban Council — Messrs. John Glasgow, J.P. (chairman), William Alexander, Joseph I. Thompson, J.P., and Hamilton Clements — were the only persons nominated on Friday of last week for the vacancies. They are, therefore, re-elected.' Returned unopposed."
